  "raw_text": "135\n\nWik lâs\n \n–\n \nweekend, end of week\n \n/ fin de semana\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nWik tnata\n)\n\nLasa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndemon, evil spirit\n \n/ demonio, espíritu maligno\n\n(\nC\nonstruct:\n \nLasika\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nSitan ai lasika aikuki\n \n–\n \nSatan with his demons\n \n/ Satanás con sus demonios\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlrw\n-\nMat\niu\n \n9:34\n):\n \nlasa\n \nnani wihtka\n \n–\n \nruler of (the) demons\n \n/ gobernante de (los) demonios\n)\n\nLasa ra kangbi sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto expel a demon\n \n/ expulsar a un demonio\n\nLasa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncancer\n,\n \n…\n \n/ cáncer\n,\n \n…\n\nLasa pruki sikniska\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nepilepsy\n \n/ epilepsia\n\n(Lit\n:\n \ndemon\n \nhitting\n \nsickness\n \n(f\nrom the belief that it\n \nis caused by demons)\n \n/ enfermedad que golpea al demonio (por la creencia de\n\nque es causada por demonios)\n)\n\nLat\n \n(\ndb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nlots\n \n/ suertes\n\nLat lulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cast lots\n \n/ echar suertes\n\nLat lulki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cast lots to see who wins, to cast lots to see what the decision is\n \n/ echar suertes\npara ver quien gana, echar suertes para ver cuál es la decisión\n\nLata\n \n(n/s,adj)\n \n–\n \noutside, the outside part, surroundings of the house\n \n/ exterior, parte de afuera, los alrededoresde la\ncasa, afuera\n\n(Construct:\n \nLatka\n)\n\nLatara\n \n(pos,adj,adj)\n \n–\n \non the outside\n \n/ en el exterior\n\nLata pahbaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyard sweeper,\n \noutside sweeper,\n \nrake\n \n/ barredora de jardín, barredora exterior, rastrillo\n\nUtla latka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyard, courtyard\n \n/ patio\n\nLatan\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nclear, visible, open, plain, apparent\n \n/ claro, visible, abierto, liso, aparente\n\nLatan apia\n \n–\n \nnot very visible, not clear, vague, absurd\n \n/\n \nno muy visible, no claro, vago, absurdo\n\nLatan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\nLatan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-1\n):\n \nWitin nani latan kaikaia sa nahki ai rayaka ra yamni munisa baha tânka aisama ba\n \n–\n \nThey must see clearly\nhow the information that you will tell them does good in their life\n \n/ Deben ver claramente cómo les beneficia en sus vidas\nla información que presentarás)\n\nLatan marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show in a clear way\n \n/ mostrar de una manera clara\n\nLatan sa\n \n–\n \nIt’s clear\n \n/ Está vacío\n\nLatan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become clear, to become visible, to become apparent\n \n/ hacerse claro, hacerse visible,\nhacerse evidente\n\nLatubaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nLahtubaia\n\nLatwan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npain, love\n \n/ dolor, amor\n\n(Construct:\n \nLaitwanka\n;\n \nLamtwanka\n;\n \nLatwanka\n)\n\nLatwan briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have a pain, to ache\n \n/ tener dolor\n\nLatwan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love, to appreciate\n \n/ amar, apreciar\n \n(see separate entry / ver entrada separada)\n\nLatwan munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hurt, to harm, to make someone feel pain\n \n/ lastimar, hacer daño, hacer que alguien\nsienta dolor\n\nLatwan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nlove\n \n/ amor\n\n(Construct:\n \nLaitwanka lâka\n;\n \nLamtwanka lâka\n;\n \nLatwanka lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nBîlam nani bara daukankam nani ba wal pana pana lamtwanka lâka ba mariks\n \n–\n \nWith your words and\ndeeds, show each other your love\n \n/ Con tus palabras y acciones, muéstrense amor)\n\nLatwan lâka kasak\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntrue love, loyal love\n \n/ amor verdadero, amor leal\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-01/22\n):\n \nUpla kum ai pânika nani wal kasak sa, bara piua karna nani ra sin witin nani ra lulki swiras sa\nkaka, latwan lâka kasak ba marikisa.\n \n–\n \nIf a person is true with their friends and doesn’t leave them in hard times\n\n(commitment), they show loyal love.\n \n/ Si una persona es fiel con sus amigos y no los deja en los momentos\ndifíciles (compromiso), muestra amor leal.)\n\nLatwan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ache\n \n/ doler\n \n(Commonly used?)\n\nLatwan wauhaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto suffer pain\n \n/ sufrir dolor\n\nLatwan yaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto harm, to make someone feel pain, to give pain\n \n/ hacer daño, hacer que alguien sienta dolor,\ndar dolor\n\nLatwan yabi rau munaia\n \n(\nbh46\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto torture\n \n/ torturar\n\nLatwan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love, to appreciate\n \n/ amar, apreciar",
